# Licensed under the terms of http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
# FEATURE 7 — what `idx:stored false` costs, and what it does not.
#
# THIS QUERY RETURNS NO ROWS, AND THAT IS THE ASSERTION.
#
# The three review fields are declared `idx:stored false`, so the index holds enough to
# find, correlate, count and sort on them, but keeps no values to hand back. luc:nestedMatch
# therefore projects nothing — an indexed-but-unstored field can be filtered on and has
# nothing to return.
#
# Note what still works, on exactly the same data:
#
#     13-nested-correlation.rq          filters same-child on reviewer + stars   -> 3 rows
#     17-nested-hierarchy-correlated.rq drills the reviewer_stars hierarchy      -> 2 rows
#     the sidebar's Reviews panel        counts every reviewer and their ratings
#
# So the knowledge graph and the index are the FILTER; the values live in the source of
# truth. data/reviews.csv is never loaded into the graph and its values are not in the
# index either — the app fetches that file directly and renders the rows itself, which is
# why a result card can show a reviewer and a rating that this query cannot produce.
#
# The trade is display staleness against index size: what the app shows is always the
# current file, and the index carries no copy of it. It does NOT buy filter freshness —
# the index is still a snapshot and must be rebuilt when the source moves.
#
# Set `idx:stored true` on field:reviewer, field:stars and field:reviewMonth in config.ttl,
# reindex, and this query starts returning three fields per matching review with no other
# change.

PREFIX luc:     <urn:jena:lucene:index#>
PREFIX schema:  <https://schema.org/>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
PREFIX rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?name ?record ?field ?value
WHERE {
    (?hit ?entity) luc:query (
        "default" "default" ""
        '{"op":">=","args":[{"property":"urn:jena:lucene:field#stars"},5]}'
        "" 20 0) .
    (?hit ?record ?field ?value) luc:nestedMatch () .
    ?entity rdfs:label|schema:name|dcterms:title ?name .
}
ORDER BY ?name ?record ?field
